					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/decibelles" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2005044); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2005044&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608670560" alt="Decibelles" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2005044)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/decibelles" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2005044); return false;" >Decibelles</a></span> <span class="odate time_1432276213 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">22 May 2015 06:30</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2300695">
									

<p>I regret not commenting on this in draft form, as the title caught my eye, but I never had the time to dedicate myself to this. Here are some things that stick out to me:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The symbols are from a large variety of sources, including Kabbalah, Hermetic mysticism, Enochian lexiurgy, European, Chinese, and Arabic alchemy, Icelandic nábrókarstafur, elder rune workings, and Daevasite fate-bindings.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This seems like a way to say &quot;It's spooky and creepy and really mysterious. Look at all these symbols that have no ties to them except how mystic they are!&quot; and it bothered me enough that I had to write this comment the moment I read it.</p>
<p>The interview with D-7920 seems&#8230; I'm not sure how to peg it. It doesn't seem believable. I read it back to myself and I can't actually imagine anyone speaking like that person does.</p>
<p>From LAVENDER CIRCLE:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Following the connection to Alagadda, LAVENDER CIRCLE attempted to correlate SCP-2890 with SCP-701. No positive correlation could be made, however ██████ ██████, the editor of the 1813 Cambridge University Press edition, is an anagram for █████ ███████; this was found to be only of marginal statistical significance.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The attempt to connect 701 with this solely because of the Alagadda connection feels immensely shoehorned, and provides absolutely nothing. You could cut this and the article would be better off for it (as does the 1274 mention; while I appreciate bringing attention to underrated skips, that thing is entirely different from this. It seems like you want to connect them because these are both dance skips?).</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We certainly live in a more sensuous, hedonistic, and open-minded society now than we had when this thing was made.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not sure what this is supposed to be saying. Is this suddenly political commentary, or does it have a political bent? What's the relation to this line with everything else? That a tophat is the reason why the world is suddenly more &quot;open-minded&quot;? You had the horror working fine before this, and with this you complicate things to the point where I'm not sure of your intentions.</p>
<p>Taking both documents into account, I have to downvote this. You go for something, you seem like you're almost there (even if some parts are a bit weird), and you end up fumbling before you can realize it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
