			<div class="content" id="post-content-2301136">
									

<blockquote>
<p>But those &quot;real world practices&quot; were not real magic.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't understand this at all. It's in the real world. It's magic. The Hermetic Order of the Golden Dawn was/is real.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Mixing them in a blender without thought will have no meaningful result.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think the premise was that the will of the magician was the important part, the symbols are only there for him to focus on. So whatever he thinks should work, will work. Besides, not mixing them also has no meaningful result in the real world.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I mean, if the procedures are going to be there, I would honestly expect what happened that lead to such measures.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There was a series of unlikely events that all individually contributed. I wrote (I thought) a fun version that everybody hated. I tried to write a less silly version, but it was really <em>boring</em>.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Boring?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Yep,&nbsp;boring.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>time: Secondary fault check circuits deactivated because of rewiring.<br />
time: A bucket of used supplies from SCP- 602 was placed in the vault pending analysis.<br />
time: Researcher [Redacted] returned SPC-2890 to containment and did not secure the lock properly but lock showed as locked to the system.<br />
time: Vibrations in the building harmonized with the resonance frequency of the bottom of the locker for 31 seconds. Artifact vibrated out of the locker. The bucket of supplies tipped over.<br />
time: Positive airflow was restored to the vault. Pressure closed the locker door (which successfully latched) and pushed the artifact into the bucket of used supplies.<br />
time: Researcher [Redacted] removed the bucket. On duty vault technician [Redacted] failed to inspect the bucket properly and permitted it to leave the vault.<br />
time: Power to the entire facility failed due to Electrician [Redacted]'s error. Researcher [Redacted] slipped and fell down the stairwell in the dark, dropping the bucket. The bucket rolled down to the ground floor, and in the darkness the hat was dislodged and rolled into the entrance gate area. Emergency power was restored.<br />
time: Hat fell into Security Officer [Redacted['s bag which had already been searched as she was going off-duty and leaving the facility.<br />
time: Entrance gate was secured until main power restored. Security Officer [Redacted] zipped up her bag while waiting for main doors to unlock.<br />
time: Main power restored. Security Officer [Redacted] left the facility.<br />
time: Security Officer [Redacted]'s bag was stolen while on the subway.</p>
</div>
</div>
