<p>I'm not saying that the luck thing should go; I'm saying that it could be expressed better and tie in the article.</p>
<p>While one breach based on coincidences might be written off as an unfortunate event, multiple breaches surrounding that particular item is less likely to be random events and one may then conjecture that the item is somehow causing those events to occur. It's a decent interpretation of chaos magic, I'd admit.</p>
<p>So yeah&#8230; I'm advocating for multiple breaches to justify the luck thing and amended procedures. By stating that those breaches are grounded in mistakes and odd coincidences (without saying what really went down) and multiple events to further the item's &quot;goals&quot;, it might better convey the message that the item is manipulating probability for its own ends.</p>

